WEBVTT

1

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.125

I was born on a small farm in

the northern region of Wall Rose.



2

00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:02.625

It was on land owned by

the noble family of Reiss.



3

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:10.792

As far back as I can remember,

I was helping around the farm.



4

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.167

But, my mother was always reading books

and not once did I see her doing housework.



5

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:22.542

She was a beautiful woman...



6

00:02:24.458 --> 00:02:27.625

At night, someone would

come for her in a wagon...



7

00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:31.750

...and she'd go off to

the city wearing fancy clothes.



8

00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:36.083

For me, that was just life as I knew it.



9

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:44.542

After I learned to read and write,

I picked up a book to imitate my mother.



10

00:02:44.542 --> 00:02:48.000

Only then did I know how alone I was.



11

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:53.000

In all the books, parents cared

about their children.



12

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.583

They talked, hugged, fought...

or so the stories went.



13

00:02:58.708 --> 00:03:02.042

I had never experienced any of those things.



14

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:08.875

One day, out of curiosity,

I decided to try hugging my mother.



15

00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:13.125

I just wanted to see what

kind of face she would make.



16

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.583

Mother!



17

00:03:20.292 --> 00:03:26.750

She ended up shoving me away, but that was

the first thing my mother ever did to me.



18

00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:30.917

That's why it made me so happy.



19

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:38.083

If only I had the courage... to kill the girl...



20

00:03:41.292 --> 00:03:45.417

Those were... the first words

my mother said to me.



21

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:52.083

After that, she left the house

and began living somewhere else.



22

00:03:53.667 --> 00:04:00.167

And then, five years ago...

One night just days after Wall Maria fell...



23

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:04.000

For the very first time, I met my father.



24

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.042

Nice to meet you, Historia.



25

00:04:07.042 --> 00:04:12.042

My name is Rod Reiss... I'm your father.



26

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:16.750

That man... He was the lord

ruling the land we lived on.



27

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.125

My mother I hadn't seen in years

looked terribly frightened.



28

00:04:23.208 --> 00:04:27.292

Historia... You'll be living with me now.



29

00:04:35.083 --> 00:04:37.708

This is a problem, Lord Reiss.



30

00:04:37.708 --> 00:04:40.833

Let's avoid acting rashly now.



31

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:45.750

Did the fall of Wall Maria

make you a little scared?



32

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:46.792

Mother!



33

00:04:46.792 --> 00:04:50.667

No! I am not the mother of that girl!



34

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:54.708

She has nothing to do with me!



35

00:04:54.708 --> 00:04:58.500

Oh? Is that true, Lord Reiss?



36

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.500

Do you really have nothing to do

with this woman or child?



37

00:05:09.625 --> 00:05:11.458

So be it...



38

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.917

These two here have nothing to do with me.



39

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:18.333

I thought that might be the case.



40

00:05:19.792 --> 00:05:21.375

What?! What are you...?



41

00:05:21.375 --> 00:05:23.917

You never existed.



42

00:05:23.917 --> 00:05:26.667

You never worked at the estate either.



43

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.708

Nobody knows who you are.



44

00:05:28.708 --> 00:05:34.292

That's not... Master!

Please tell them that's not true!



45

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:36.542

Mother...



46

00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:39.833

If only...



47

00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:42.625

If only I never had you!



48

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:53.792

Those were my mother's last words.



49

00:05:58.375 --> 00:06:00.167

Wait.



50

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:05.500

Moments before I was to be killed,

my father proposed an idea.



51

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:12.042

That if I were to be sent far away and live out

a quiet life, perhaps they could spare me.



52

00:06:12.042 --> 00:06:16.125

Your name will be Christa Lenz.



53

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.333

Please forgive me for everything.



54

00:06:27.333 --> 00:06:31.625

In order to protect you, I had no other choice.



55

00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:34.333

F-Father...



56

00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:37.667

I was always thinking about you.



57

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:42.042

I've always dreamed of the day

I could hold you like this.



58

00:06:42.042 --> 00:06:46.333

You're special... Royal blood runs through you.



59

00:06:48.458 --> 00:06:50.625

It... does?



60

00:06:50.625 --> 00:06:53.625

That's right, Historia.



61

00:06:53.625 --> 00:06:57.583

Our Reiss family is the true royal line.



62

00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:03.083

And because you're special, you're the one

and only person who can save all of humanity.



63

00:07:03.083 --> 00:07:05.583

Now, let us go, Historia.



64

00:07:05.583 --> 00:07:08.417

To the place it all began...



65

00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:13.792

Sannes!



66

00:07:13.792 --> 00:07:16.125

Are you... all right?!



67

00:07:17.958 --> 00:07:20.417

Hey, don't tell me...



68

00:07:20.417 --> 00:07:23.208

You didn't tell them anything, right?



69

00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:25.708

Our loyalty to the King is more--



70

00:07:26.958 --> 00:07:28.083

Sannes!



71

00:07:28.083 --> 00:07:30.875

I can't stand to hear your voice anymore!



72

00:07:30.875 --> 00:07:34.333

You've betrayed me since the very beginning!



73

00:07:36.333 --> 00:07:38.625

To think how I trusted you!



74

00:07:38.625 --> 00:07:41.708

Sannes! He never told us anything.



75

00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:44.542

In fact, we never questioned him.



76

00:07:45.875 --> 00:07:51.083

We threatened Ralph with a knife and

forced him to read this script that I wrote.



77

00:07:51.083 --> 00:07:52.792

That's all.



78

00:07:58.333 --> 00:08:00.125

Then...



79

00:08:00.125 --> 00:08:01.833

I...



80

00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:04.583

I betrayed the King?



81

00:08:08.625 --> 00:08:11.542

Y-You devils!



82

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:20.708

I'm not trying to deny it, but... I'm sure

Nick thought the same thing about you.



83

00:08:20.708 --> 00:08:23.250

That's why I said what I did.



84

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:26.333

That I was beginning to feel sorry for you.



85

00:08:26.333 --> 00:08:30.875

Look at how pathetic you are!

Grown-ass men wailing and crying!



86

00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:33.958

It serves you right, morons!



87

00:08:33.958 --> 00:08:38.542

See how you like spending the rest

of your life shitting in a tiny cell!



88

00:08:38.542 --> 00:08:40.125

See you.



89

00:08:41.167 --> 00:08:43.125

Next in line...



90

00:08:44.833 --> 00:08:49.500

This role of ours... There's an order to it.



91

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:55.917

When one's role is done,

another steps in to start the act again.



92

00:08:55.917 --> 00:08:59.792

And thus, the world can never be rid of it.



93

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:04.667

Good luck, Hange.



94

00:09:07.208 --> 00:09:08.708

Section Commander?



95

00:09:23.667 --> 00:09:27.250

Sorry... I made a mess.



96

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.375

There was a cockroach.



97

00:09:29.375 --> 00:09:35.083

I see... Just one kick of yours

should've blasted it to bits.



98

00:09:35.083 --> 00:09:37.292

It's about time you fill them in.



99

00:09:37.292 --> 00:09:40.625

Oh... Yeah, I should.



100

00:09:40.625 --> 00:09:42.708

Eren will be eaten?!



101

00:09:42.708 --> 00:09:43.958

Yeah.



102

00:09:43.958 --> 00:09:47.458

Eren remembered a conversation

that went like this...



103

00:09:47.458 --> 00:09:49.958

Do you resent me for it?



104

00:09:49.958 --> 00:09:51.750

I'm not sure...



105

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:55.000

I... don't know.



106

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.542

You probably didn't want

to eat a human either...



107

00:09:58.542 --> 00:10:04.000

Speculating based on that, Ymir was a

Titan wandering alone outside the wall.



108

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.417

Bertholdt, Reiner, and Annie

had a comrade that she ate.



109

00:10:08.417 --> 00:10:12.500

When a Titan eats someone,

they don't change back into a human.



110

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:15.833

But what if a Titan ate

one of Reiner's comrades?



111

00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:19.417

They're humans who can transform into Titans.



112

00:10:19.417 --> 00:10:24.958

In other words, if a Titan eats someone with

that power, they revert back into a human.



113

00:10:24.958 --> 00:10:28.792

Furthermore, they obtain

the power of those they eat.



114

00:10:28.792 --> 00:10:34.750

In the other day's battle, Reiner was

throwing Titans at Eren, who had escaped.



115

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.708

Eren has the power to

control Titans with his scream.



116

00:10:38.708 --> 00:10:41.750

He was trying to snatch

that power with those Titans.



117

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:47.500

In that case, Eren is just a vessel

who is bound to be replaced.



118

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:54.083

Basically, if the government has a Titan

of their own, they'll be the one to eat Eren.



119

00:10:56.375 --> 00:10:57.750

Calm down.



120

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:02.292

Even if you go on a rampage,

they're not going to give Eren back to us.



121

00:11:02.292 --> 00:11:06.125

Anyways, we head for

the lands of this Rod Reiss.



122

00:11:06.125 --> 00:11:08.125

Get ready to leave at once.



123

00:11:08.125 --> 00:11:09.250

Yes, sir!



124

00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:16.292

I'll go tell Erwin what we learned

about the Reiss family.



125

00:11:16.292 --> 00:11:18.750

I'm sure he's waiting to hear from us.



126

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.000

Right.



127

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.292

We can meet up on Reiss' land.

Hear from me at the usual spot.



128

00:11:27.958 --> 00:11:32.042

Excuse me. Commander Erwin,

Pyxis is here for you.



129

00:11:32.042 --> 00:11:33.167

The commander?



130

00:11:33.167 --> 00:11:36.250

Yes, he wants to see you.



131

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:38.708

Let him in.



132

00:11:38.708 --> 00:11:39.833

Sir!



133

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:47.667

Sorry about the late visit.



134

00:11:47.667 --> 00:11:50.833

I just couldn't stand still, you see.



135

00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:53.292

I finished reading your letter.



136

00:11:53.292 --> 00:11:56.083

I came with some thoughts of my own.



137

00:11:58.208 --> 00:12:02.542

But first I need to ask... Are you serious?



138

00:12:03.542 --> 00:12:05.583

Yes.



139

00:12:05.583 --> 00:12:10.583

In order to retake Wall Maria,

we'll overthrow the government.



140

00:12:19.833 --> 00:12:22.875

I knew this would happen one day.



141

00:12:22.875 --> 00:12:28.542

This cramped world can only hold people

for so long before they begin to lash out.



142

00:12:28.542 --> 00:12:34.417

And when that time came, I'd have to

point my gun at the King as well.



143

00:12:35.458 --> 00:12:42.292

If my guess proves correct, this plan will not

require military forces to take action.



144

00:12:42.292 --> 00:12:45.375

Nor should it be necessary for anyone to die.



145

00:12:45.375 --> 00:12:51.917

Oh? Do tell me then.

Is such a method possible?



146

00:12:51.917 --> 00:12:56.667

However, the groundwork for this

to happen is not quite ready.



147

00:12:56.667 --> 00:13:02.750

And if everything is not in order, me and

everyone else will be hanged, no doubt.



148

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:05.250

Oh, that's all?



149

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:08.500

In other words, it's another huge gamble.



150

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:11.750

It seems I may be a betting man.



151

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.875

The news should come shortly.



152

00:13:13.875 --> 00:13:18.750

Until it arrives, I'd like you to hear

a story regarding my childhood.



153

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:20.333

Hmm?



154

00:13:20.333 --> 00:13:23.750

My father... He was a teacher.



155

00:13:23.958 --> 00:13:28.958

"An Intelligent Titan is conceived when a Pure Titan

lacking intelligence consumes some other Intelligent

Titan. By consuming an Intelligent Titan, it gains

consciousness as well as the consumed Titan's powers."



156

00:13:34.875 --> 00:13:36.250

What in the world?



157

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.625

Section Commander, that was--



158

00:13:37.625 --> 00:13:40.000

Yeah, I know.



159

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.917

Excuse me!



160

00:13:44.917 --> 00:13:46.083

Erwin...



161

00:13:48.208 --> 00:13:50.833

I thought as much.



162

00:13:50.833 --> 00:13:54.750

My gamble was right after all, Commander.



163

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.625

One of the First Interior Squad confessed.



164

00:13:57.625 --> 00:14:00.542

The current royal family is a fraud.



165

00:14:00.542 --> 00:14:03.542

Reiss is the true royal family.



166

00:14:03.542 --> 00:14:05.208

My word!



167

00:14:05.208 --> 00:14:09.625

Right now, Squad Levi is underway

rescuing Eren and Historia.



168

00:14:09.625 --> 00:14:14.875

Once they're recovered, we'll have

Historia Reiss enthroned as Queen.



169

00:14:14.875 --> 00:14:17.917

As one possessing the true royal blood.



170

00:14:19.333 --> 00:14:23.458

And you'll force the makeshift

King to relinquish the crown?



171

00:14:23.458 --> 00:14:25.583

To the true Queen...



172

00:14:25.583 --> 00:14:29.542

Without spilling any blood,

we will overthrow the government.



173

00:14:29.542 --> 00:14:35.458

And in front of the people, we'll reveal that

the system as they know it has all been a lie.



174

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:41.375

Very well. I'll back your plan.



175

00:14:41.375 --> 00:14:46.583

However, whether or not it should be

carried out is not for us to decide.



176

00:14:46.583 --> 00:14:49.458

You understand that, don't you, Erwin?



177

00:14:49.458 --> 00:14:51.958

Of course, Commander.



178

00:14:57.208 --> 00:15:00.000

Did anything come of the Reiss investigation?



179

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.375

I found out as much as I could.



180

00:15:03.375 --> 00:15:06.625

From all that I learned,

one curious incident stuck out.



181

00:15:06.625 --> 00:15:08.833

Incident?



182

00:15:08.833 --> 00:15:12.708

Commander Erwin! The Interior Squad

demands you turn yourself in!



183

00:15:13.708 --> 00:15:18.875

They're making a scene in the middle of

the city that you organized a murder!



184

00:15:18.875 --> 00:15:22.208

It seems the enemy's been

making plans of their own.



185

00:15:22.208 --> 00:15:24.125

Hange, get far from here.



186

00:15:24.125 --> 00:15:27.125

Huh?! What are you planning to do?



187

00:15:27.125 --> 00:15:30.333

I need to be the face of the Scout Regiment.



188

00:15:30.333 --> 00:15:33.375

You should act at your own discretion.



189

00:15:33.375 --> 00:15:36.875

Furthermore, the next commander

of the Scout Regiment...



190

00:15:36.875 --> 00:15:39.417

Hange Zoë, it's you.



191

00:15:40.458 --> 00:15:42.667

The Scouts are in your hands.



192

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.167

Hey, he's here.



193

00:15:49.167 --> 00:15:50.708

It's Erwin.



194

00:15:55.917 --> 00:15:59.458

I take it you know who this is, Erwin?



195

00:16:00.542 --> 00:16:03.083

The boss of Reeves Company.



196

00:16:03.083 --> 00:16:04.833

Mr. Dimo Reeves.



197

00:16:04.833 --> 00:16:11.042

Yesterday, and in this very place, Eren Jaeger

was abducted by underlings of Reeves.



198

00:16:11.042 --> 00:16:16.458

However... that was all a mere scheme

between the Scouts and Reeves Company



199

00:16:16.458 --> 00:16:21.333

in order to evade handing over

Eren Jaeger to the government.



200

00:16:21.333 --> 00:16:27.417

And then... when Reeves was no longer needed,

they killed the man to keep him from talking.



201

00:16:27.417 --> 00:16:31.875

The murderer is still at large

and must be holed up with Eren.



202

00:16:31.875 --> 00:16:34.125

What a convenient story that is.



203

00:16:34.125 --> 00:16:40.292

What you scoundrels are doing... It's the same

as monopolizing Eren's power for yourself.



204

00:16:40.292 --> 00:16:44.417

And that act violates Clause Six

of the Charter of Humanity.



205

00:16:44.417 --> 00:16:46.958

You know which that one is, don't you?



206

00:16:46.958 --> 00:16:52.458

To prioritize one's own gain over the safety

and longevity of humanity, yes?



207

00:16:52.458 --> 00:16:54.083

That's right.



208

00:16:54.083 --> 00:17:00.167

Therefore, in acknowledgment of violating

said law, all Scouts are to be apprehended!



209

00:17:00.167 --> 00:17:01.625

Old Man...



210

00:17:08.542 --> 00:17:12.000

You think the fat cats will finally be satisfied?



211

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.917

I bet Reeves would be glad to know

he proved useful in the end.



212

00:17:15.917 --> 00:17:18.000

There's still Levi to deal with...



213

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:21.000

I told you, he'll show up on his own.



214

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.417

We'll crush him when the time comes.



215

00:17:29.333 --> 00:17:31.375

What do we do now?!



216

00:17:33.708 --> 00:17:35.000

May I have a moment?



217

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.083

Hmm?



218

00:17:40.583 --> 00:17:43.500

Get away from my husband, you lowlife!



219

00:17:45.125 --> 00:17:47.500

In the battle of Trost District,



220

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:52.167

Mr. Reeves delayed the evacuation

by trying to take along his wealth.



221

00:17:53.583 --> 00:17:56.667

So what?! Are you saying he deserved to die?!



222

00:17:56.667 --> 00:18:02.208

However... given the current situation

with Trost on the verge of collapse...



223

00:18:02.208 --> 00:18:05.833

He planted his feet in the city,

and using any means possible...



224

00:18:05.833 --> 00:18:11.167

...he aided those with no place to go

while striving to revive the city.



225

00:18:11.167 --> 00:18:15.958

Except, by somebody's hands

that dream was extinguished.



226

00:18:15.958 --> 00:18:19.458

I promise you... I will avenge him.



227

00:18:29.583 --> 00:18:33.667

My father... He was a teacher.



228

00:18:33.667 --> 00:18:36.500

One day, we were learning history.



229

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:39.458

To protect themselves from the Titans,



230

00:18:39.458 --> 00:18:44.250

humanity took refuge within the walls

and realized 100 years of peace.



231

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:51.042

In doing so, any records of our

earlier past were lost for all of time.



232

00:18:51.042 --> 00:18:53.167

That's what we're all taught.



233

00:18:54.167 --> 00:19:01.000

However, I... having doubts of my own,

asked my father a question.



234

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:07.292

My father evaded answering the question

and ended class as normal.



235

00:19:07.292 --> 00:19:09.458

But...



236

00:19:09.458 --> 00:19:14.042

After we got home,

my father answered my question.



237

00:19:14.042 --> 00:19:16.167

He said the history books

given by the government



238

00:19:16.167 --> 00:19:20.083

were full of contradictions and mysteries.



239

00:19:20.083 --> 00:19:26.625

My father continued to tell me more,

and even as a child, I was astounded.



240

00:19:26.625 --> 00:19:33.792

There's a reason he didn't tell that story to the

entire class, but I wasn't smart enough to know.



241

00:19:35.125 --> 00:19:38.458

I'd been telling the other

kids my father's story,



242

00:19:38.458 --> 00:19:42.500

and one day, the Military Police

came to question me.



243

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:48.667

My father didn't come home that day...

He died in some accident in a faraway town.



244

00:19:48.667 --> 00:19:53.208

Based on what I knew,

my father was killed by the government.



245

00:19:55.083 --> 00:19:59.625

One hundred and seven years ago...

Humanity that fled into these walls...



246

00:19:59.625 --> 00:20:04.250

The King had altered their memories

to make them easy to rule.



247

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:06.542

That was my father's theory.



248

00:20:06.542 --> 00:20:13.292

Oh? Because if they hadn't done that,

civilization within the walls could never succeed?



249

00:20:13.292 --> 00:20:14.583

Yes.



250

00:20:14.583 --> 00:20:17.458

Ever since I was a child, I've been thinking...



251

00:20:17.458 --> 00:20:22.625

Why did my father have to die for

nothing more than getting close to the truth?



252

00:20:22.625 --> 00:20:28.000

Even those in the government would

believe what they're doing is just.



253

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:32.417

However, I realized one thing about them...



254

00:20:32.417 --> 00:20:38.875

What they're trying to protect is not humanity,

but their gardens, houses, and lands.



255

00:20:38.875 --> 00:20:46.250

Rather, if anyone dares threaten their authority,

they'll be extinguished, whoever they are.



256

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:51.083

In the end, there was nothing

to justify my father's death.



257

00:20:51.083 --> 00:20:56.917

My father was killed by human greed...

And by the foolishness of his own son.



258

00:20:56.917 --> 00:21:02.417

Before I knew it, my father's theory

became truth inside my heart.



259

00:21:02.417 --> 00:21:08.250

Now, my mission in life... It's to prove

my father's theory once and for all.



260

00:21:12.167 --> 00:21:15.417

The Scout Regiment murdered a civilian!



261

00:21:15.417 --> 00:21:19.333

Some of them have fled capture!

They're still on the loose!



262

00:21:19.333 --> 00:21:23.208

If you spot any of these persons,

report it immediately!



263

00:21:23.208 --> 00:21:25.000

Told you, didn't I?



264

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:29.542

They're the ones who had that Titan battle here

and destroyed practically everything!



265

00:21:29.542 --> 00:21:33.542

I bet they're planning to use that

Eren monster to wipe us out!



266

00:21:36.667 --> 00:21:39.583

Captain, we bought the supplies.



267

00:21:39.583 --> 00:21:42.125

The Military Police were handing out these.



268

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:47.875

If this is true, the Scouts will be disbanded.



269

00:21:47.875 --> 00:21:50.542

I heard they'll be hunting for us tonight.



270

00:21:50.542 --> 00:21:56.458

They're also putting guards on all the vital roads,

and it's impossible to get through without a pass.



271

00:21:56.458 --> 00:21:58.500

Captain, what now?



272

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:00.500

If we don't hurry, Eren...



273

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.083

Calm down.



274

00:22:02.083 --> 00:22:04.292

They're using a wagon.



275

00:22:04.292 --> 00:22:08.000

It'll take at least a day

to reach Reiss' territory.



276

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:11.750

We'll have to use that time

to come up with a plan.



277

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:14.000

Captain, I hear footsteps.



278

00:22:16.167 --> 00:22:18.167

They're coming this way.



279

00:23:57.542 --> 00:23:59.542

Those who throw away their life...



280

00:23:59.542 --> 00:24:01.667

Those who believe in justice...



281

00:24:01.667 --> 00:24:03.917

Those who protect the city...



282

00:24:03.917 --> 00:24:09.833

Courage which swells up from memories

gives people the courage to fight.



283

00:24:09.833 --> 00:24:12.096

Next episode: "Trust."

